<title>USA: NYMEX July crude oil breaches key support.</title>
<headline>NYMEX July crude oil breaches key support.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>NYMEX July crude oil futures prices fell to the contract's lowest level in nine months at midday Friday, hammered by speculative and trade selling in what turned quickly into a bear market in the past week.</p>
<p>At 1342 EDT, July crude was down 53 cents at $19.13 a barrel, falling to below the April 4 low of $19.18 that had been considered crude's most significant near support.</p>
